# CR 707.2, 708.2a. A face-down permanent is a 2/2 creature with no name, and a copy takes exactly what it copies, so a
# token that is a copy of one is a face-up 2/2 creature with no name, no types beyond creature and no abilities. The
# engine used to refuse to create it: "a card or token needs a nonempty name" stopped the game as Three Steps Ahead
# resolved.
#
# Turn 1 is the Abhorrent Oculus opening the other manifest scenarios use: a Wheel of Fortune off a Black Lotus fills
# the graveyard, six of those cards are exiled for the Oculus. On Bot2's upkeep it manifests dread and Guerrilla Gorilla
# goes onto the battlefield face down. On turn 3 Bot1 casts Three Steps Ahead for its copy mode ({U} and {3}) at the
# face-down creature, which a script names as the failure report prints it: its controller, its zone and no name.
#
# It stops as Bot1 declares attackers, with the face-down card and the nameless token side by side, to
# picture how each is drawn. #1 is the
# face-down Gorilla, on the battlefield since turn 2; #2 is the token, which arrived this turn.

